    stem: "Photograph A on Paper X shows the plan of the Temple of Zeus at Olympia.",
    questionText: "Describe the sculptural decoration of this temple.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"questionTotal"}, totalMarks: 20,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "The main decorative features are the two pediments and the twelve sculpted metopes over the entrance, (all made of marble)", marks: null },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "point", verbatim: "On the east pediment there are figures representing the start of the chariot race of Pelops", marks: null },
    { id: "r-3", kind: "point", verbatim: "The more famous west pediment shows Apollo calming the riot of Centaurs at the Lapith wedding", marks: null },
    { id: "r-4", kind: "point", verbatim: "He dominates the scene which includes the women being manhandled by Centaurs, writhing figures and, in the corners, reclining women", marks: null },
    { id: "r-5", kind: "point", verbatim: "It is a very successful composition where all the figures inter-relate", marks: null },
    { id: "r-6", kind: "point", verbatim: "The twelve metopes show each of the tasks of Heracles, again, a mix of quiet and action-packed scenes", marks: null },
    { id: "r-7", kind: "point", verbatim: "The one shown is the Golden Apples of the Hesperides being handed over by Atlas to Herakles, with a stately Athena looking on", marks: null },
    { id: "r-8", kind: "point", verbatim: "Three aspects of the sculptures fully described – east and west pediments and metopes: (7, 7, 6.) Reference could also be made to the later statue of Zeus", marks: null },
    ],
