    questionText: "Explain the ways in which this sculpture is typical of its period.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"questionTotal"}, totalMarks: 30,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "This sculpture, known as the Anavysos Kouros is typical of its period in several ways", marks: null },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "point", verbatim: "It is a young, male figure standing in a very rigid pose with hands clenched by his sides and his left foot stepped forward, so it is a typical archaic kouros", marks: null },
    { id: "r-3", kind: "point", verbatim: "Also, it has very stylised hair carved in detailed patterns and not very naturalistic", marks: null },
    { id: "r-4", kind: "point", verbatim: "His face is also very symmetrical with the archaic smile", marks: null },
    { id: "r-5", kind: "point", verbatim: "The elements that show that he is late archaic include: the fact that his muscles are contoured rather than shown by lines and grooves, especially around his chest and shoulders: his appearance of weight bearing is more realistic than earlier kouroi; his arms and legs are more realistic looking than earlier kouroi and his face is less flat than earlier examples", marks: null },
    { id: "r-6", kind: "point", verbatim: "He is definitely archaic but sculpted at the point where artists were moving towards a more realistic style, using the observation of reality", marks: null },
    ],
